Report #124: "Haunt can only apply CoE or CoA, would like it to do both
please." Haunt seeds the target with the Affliction DoT set including Curse
of Agony and Curse of the Elements, but the engine kept only one of the two.

Root cause, read not guessed: Aura::CanStackWith
(src/server/game/Spells/Auras/SpellAuras.cpp) rejects a new aura when
IsAuraExclusiveBySpecificPerCasterWith() says the existing one conflicts and
the caster is the same. SpellInfo::GetSpellSpecific() maps every spell with
DispelType CURSE to SPELL_SPECIFIC_CURSE (SpellInfo.cpp:2136), so Curse of
Agony and Curse of the Elements -- different curse *types* (doom/agony DoT vs
spell-damage-taken debuff, with no overlapping effects) -- were treated as
exclusive per caster. The cast itself succeeds; the second aura application
replaces the first. This is engine stacking logic, not module application
order, and it is not a spell_group rule (the curse groups in
acore_world.spell_group cover Immolate/UA and spell-damage debuffs, not the
Agony/Elements pair), so no data-only fix exists: GetSpellSpecific() is
computed from DispelType in code, not read from a table.

Fix: an exception in Aura::CanStackWith -- if the two spells are the Curse of
Agony chain (first spell 980) and the Curse of the Elements chain (first
spell 1490), in either order, the pair can stack. Chain heads are resolved
through sSpellMgr->GetFirstSpellInChain so higher ranks (47867 Agony,
47865 Elements) behave identically. Every other curse pairing keeps vanilla
one-curse-per-caster exclusivity, and cross-caster behaviour is unchanged
(two different warlocks could already curse both).

Touching an engine stacking rule for a specific pair is deliberately narrow:
the alternative (handing CoE out as a different DispelType via spell_dbc)
would make the curse dispellable as magic and change dispel behaviour realm-
wide. The module hook is Aura::CanStackWith because both auras are applied
from the same Haunt-triggered path (LivingGear_ClassPerks.cpp,
TryWarlockAfflictionOnCast) and no module hook sits between the engine's
stack check and the aura list.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Auras/SpellAuras.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Auras/SpellAuras.cpp
@@ -1973,6 +1973,23 @@
             return true;
     }

+    // Living Gear core-patch 0034 (report #124): Curse of Agony (980 chain)
+    // and Curse of the Elements (1490 chain) are different curse types --
+    // agony is a doom/agony DoT, elements is a spell-damage-taken debuff --
+    // but both carry DispelType CURSE, so GetSpellSpecific() maps both to
+    // SPELL_SPECIFIC_CURSE and the per-caster rule below let a Haunt-seeded
+    // pair keep only one of them. The two effects do not overlap, so allow
+    // exactly this pair to coexist from the same caster; every other curse
+    // pairing keeps the vanilla one-curse-per-caster exclusivity.
+    {
+        bool const newIsAgony = sSpellMgr->GetFirstSpellInChain(GetId()) == 980;
+        bool const newIsElements = sSpellMgr->GetFirstSpellInChain(GetId()) == 1490;
+        bool const existIsAgony = sSpellMgr->GetFirstSpellInChain(existingSpellInfo->Id) == 980;
+        bool const existIsElements = sSpellMgr->GetFirstSpellInChain(existingSpellInfo->Id) == 1490;
+        if ((newIsAgony && existIsElements) || (newIsElements && existIsAgony))
+            return true;
+    }
+
     // check spell specific stack rules
     if (m_spellInfo->IsAuraExclusiveBySpecificWith(existingSpellInfo)
             || (sameCaster && m_spellInfo->IsAuraExclusiveBySpecificPerCasterWith(existingSpellInfo)))
